        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A treadmill is good for weight loss when you use it often,
            keep it up for months and let your diet do its share.</strong> Brisk walking on a
            moderate incline, hands off the rails, most days of the week, is a better plan for most
            people than hard running a few times a week.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ignore the calorie display as a food allowance, watch for appetite creeping up and for the
            rest of your day becoming more sedentary, and judge progress weekly rather than daily.
